payload.text:
Build evidence for basicly-p71af3r, part 2 of 2.

Exemption, not a waiver: skill_pairing.UNPAIRED_EXEMPTIONS lists agent-mail because a top-level session talks to its peer sessions and a lane role never does; that list is the pairing rule's own mechanism.

nosec B404 B603 B607 on mail_root.git(): the argv is always the literal "git" plus fixed subcommand strings (rev-parse, check-ignore -q --) and the fixed relative path .orchestrator/agent-mail-root; no message text, agent name or resource reaches it. The folder a person passes to init is only the working directory.

Concurrency tests that can fail, each run against a deliberately broken copy:
- delivery that overwrites (rename onto the final name) fails test_concurrent_senders_with_one_clock_reading_lose_no_message for both the link and the no-link path;
- the no-link fallback without its reservation fails the no-link case;
- writing straight into new/ fails test_a_reader_never_sees_a_half_written_message. The first version of that test, with the reader in a thread, passed against this broken copy; it was rewritten with the reader in a separate process and then failed;
- a check-then-create lock fails test_a_lock_has_exactly_one_winner_among_concurrent_processes;
- the old locale stdin reader fails test_a_non_ascii_body_survives_a_non_utf8_locale with garbled text.
The real script passed tests/test_agent_mail.py (23 tests) 5 runs in a row, and ran by hand on Python 3.12.

Gate refusals fixed at the cause, none bypassed: ruff (18 style findings), bandit (B404, B603, B607 on the git call), module-size (5234 tokens over 4000; split into agent_mail.py, mail_root.py, mail_store.py), projection-skills (a stray temporary pyright json under .agents/skills that the hook run created), and ruff format rewriting "except (A, B):" into 3.14-only syntax (clauses split; a test parses the modules with feature_version 3.12).

Unproven: CI runs tests/test_agent_mail.py on Linux only; see the adjacent record for Windows and macOS. A lock has exactly one winner only when every agent of a folder uses this script; the skill text says to move all agents of a folder in one step.
